### 🎨 CSS‑only rotating card (hover)

Below is a **complete, copy‑and‑paste ready** example that shows a card with a front and a back side.  
When you hover over the card it flips around the Y‑axis (you can change it to X‑axis if you prefer).

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card – Hover</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣  Container ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
  width: 300px;          /* card width */
  height: 200px;         /* card height */
  perspective: 1000px;   /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
  margin: 50px auto;     /* center horizontally */
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣  Card (the flipping element) ---------- */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* keep children in 3D space */
  transition: transform 0.8s ease;/* smooth animation */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣  Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);     /* flip 180° around Y axis */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣  Card faces ---------- */
.card-face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* hide backside when turned */
  border-radius: 10px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣  Front side ---------- */
.card-front {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff9a9e 0%, #fad0c4 100%);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #fff;
}

/* ---------- 6️⃣  Back side ---------- */
.card-back {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #a18cd1 0%, #fbc2eb 100%);
  transform: rotateY(180deg);      /* start rotated so it appears on flip */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  color: #fff;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-face card-front">
      Front
    </div>
    <div class="card-face card-back">
      Back
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

---

#### 🔧 How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| 1️⃣ | `.card-wrapper` sets `perspective` | Gives depth to the 3D transform |
| 2️⃣ | `.card` has `transform-style: preserve-3d` | Keeps child elements in 3D space |
| 3️⃣ | `.card:hover` applies `rotateY(180deg)` | Flips the card on hover |
| 4️⃣ | `.card-face` uses `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the backside when it’s turned away |
| 5️⃣ | `.card-front` is the visible side initially | Styled with gradient & centered text |
| 6️⃣ | `.card-back` starts rotated 180° | So it becomes visible after the flip |

---

#### 📐 Customisation tips

| Property | Where to change | What it does |
|----------|-----------------|--------------|
| `width / height` | `.card-wrapper` | Size of the card |
| `perspective` | `.card-wrapper` | Depth of the 3D effect (higher → more subtle) |
| `transition` | `.card` | Speed & easing of the flip |
| `rotateY(180deg)` | `.card:hover` | Change to `rotateX(180deg)` for vertical flip |
| `backface-visibility` | `.card-face` | Keep it hidden for clean flip |
| Gradients / colors | `.card-front` / `.card-back` | Change the look of each side |

---

#### 🎯 Use‑case ideas

- Product showcase cards (front: image, back: description)
- Profile cards (front: photo, back: bio)
- Quiz cards (front: question, back: answer)
- Interactive menu items

---

#### 🚀 Quick test

1. Copy the entire code block above.  
2. Paste it into a new file called `index.html`.  
3. Open the file in your browser.  
4. Hover over the card – it should flip!

Feel free to tweak the dimensions, colors, or add more content inside `.card-front` and `.card-back`. Happy coding!
